  "details": "I want to make separate game modes for my game maps that I'm working on, however in public instances players will want to join for the sake of playing the main game. I'd like to be able to make it so players have more control over the game when an instance is private or friends+ so that the game can be more configurable without the worry that it would be misused in a public instance.\n\nI don't think being able to detect invite/invite+/friends/friends+ is necessary or even good, I just think a bool for \"IsPublicInstance\" would be beneficial, and would make more \"Staff only\" rooms in other maps be available to users in a non-public-intrusive way",
